It responds negatively to 'zu', its short beginnings and contractions, and
to u immediately following z across a token boundary.  German separable
verb particles strengthen that last response.  Short su spellings, s|u,
accented u after s/z, and English 'too' receive weaker negative values.
Longer words are not treated as these short fragments.  Only the current
alphabetic word is carried, and it is reset between documents.
