"""Predict opening-token levels and smaller command-line syntax responses.

Training showed an opening transient whose sign depends on token spelling,
and positive responses on shell switches and subcommands. This approximation
uses whitespace, punctuation, digits, articles, case and leading spaces at a
document's first token. Elsewhere it recognizes common tool/subcommand pairs
and alphabetic switches after a hyphen, retaining tool context for 24 tokens
or until a newline. It omits irregular word-specific responses.
"""

READS = ()

# Common command-line tools and the verbs used as their subcommands.
