"""Use recent vocabulary to recognize de/di and Romance d-apostrophe forms.

Word frequencies identify the recent language; a diagnostic nearby word can
also reveal a borrowed phrase. No model weights or token-id table are used.
The response is strong for French/Romanian de and Italian di, weaker for
Spanish/Portuguese de, and negative for Dutch/Scandinavian de or non-Italian di.
A word-initial d (also D or -d) followed by an apostrophe has its own response,
as does the colon in a document-opening Title: label. Other tokens get zero;
rare non-Latin fragment responses are not modeled.
