"""Approximate a sparse token-formatting signal.

Standalone spaces after real or written-out \\n line breaks are strongly
positive. Real line breaks get an early-document boost. Spaces after quotes,
indentation with 4k+1 trailing spaces, nonbreaking-space/backtick formatting,
and repeated escape slashes receive smaller positive responses. Ordinary
text is near zero. At document starts, use coarse case/spacing classes and
recognize an initial empty // comment, rather than memorize vocabulary.
