What it does, in plain terms:
  * Positive on the word right after "as" in the fixed phrases "as of" and "as such"
    (strongest on "of": "As of June ..."); weaker on "as is", "as to", "as for".
  * Negative on words built on the root "vas-" of blood vessels: "vascular",
